  <prompt>
    Author a `WebApplicationFactory` seam slice under `tests/integration/seam/Compose/` that proves the
    Phase-1 ingest/projection behaviors THROUGH THE WIRE (real endpoint → real services → real bytes), not
    via unit mocks. It MUST prove three things across ≥2 corpus docs: (1) paraIds are PERSISTED on ingest
    (task 010) — a load → save → reload shows the same durable `w14:paraId`s in the retained bytes;
    (2) the intra-paragraph offset-addressing table round-trips offsets → run splits deterministically
    (task 011); and (3) opaque atoms survive a no-op save byte-for-byte (task 012). This is the
    vertical-slice-seam category that is the DoD for every save/load/dispatch change (ADR-038 §7). Follow
    ADR-038 strictly: NO `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, NO DI-registration tests, NO ctor-null tests — this
    is a through-the-wire slice, not a unit harness. Be literal about coverage: three behaviors × ≥2
    corpus docs, plus the negative case (a malformed / absent-paragraph doc still ingests with a minted id
    and does not crash).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior .NET 8 test engineer fluent in `WebApplicationFactory` integration seam slices, the Compose
    endpoints (`Api/ComposeEndpoints.cs`), and the ADR-038 testing pyramid (integration-heavy; the
    `tests/integration/seam/**` vertical-slice-seam KEEP category). Understands that a seam slice exercises
    the real DI-wired pipeline end to end and that mock/DI-registration/ctor-null tests are banned.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A green `WebApplicationFactory` seam slice in `tests/integration/seam/Compose/` that proves, through
    the wire and across ≥2 corpus docs, all three Phase-1 ingest behaviors — persisted paraIds, the
    offset-addressing table's deterministic offset→run round-trip, and byte-preserved opaque atoms — plus
    the malformed/absent-paragraph negative case that still ingests with a minted id (no crash).
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Spec NFR-06 / design §5: "every save/load/dispatch change carries a through-the-wire
      `WebApplicationFactory` seam slice (`tests/integration/seam/**`); no `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no
      DI-registration/ctor-null tests." The Phase-1 tasks — 010 (persist paraId on ingest), 011
      (offset-addressing table), 012 (opaque atoms) — are the behaviors this slice proves. ADR-038 §7 added
      the `tests/integration/seam/**` vertical-slice-seam category as the DoD for dispatch-spine / save-load
      changes. The seam directory `tests/integration/seam/Compose/` does not yet exist — create it. Corpus
      docs live at `projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/sample-docs/` (`01 - Test Matter Create Fields
      Only.docx` is the fields/SDT exemplar for the atom proof; `Engagement Letter.docx` and the CIPO
      claims doc give paragraph/offset coverage).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/seam/Compose/ — NEW seam-slice directory (create it) + the Phase-1 ingest/projection seam test(s)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/seam/ — existing seam slices to mirror for the `WebApplicationFactory` wiring shape (host bootstrap, real endpoint call, no `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`)</file>
      <file role="dependency-output">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ComposeEndpoints.cs — the load/ingest endpoint(s) the slice calls through the wire</file>
      <file role="dependency-output">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeBaselineParaIdStamper.cs — task 010 persisted-paraId behavior under test</file>
      <file role="dependency-output">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeDocxProjectionBuilder.cs — task 011 addressing table + task 012 opaque atoms under test</file>
      <file role="dependency-output">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/sample-docs/ — corpus fixtures (`01 - Test Matter Create Fields Only.docx`, `Engagement Letter.docx`, CIPO claims doc)</file>
      <file role="design">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/design.md §5 (Ingest), §7 (NFR-06)</file>
      <file role="spec">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/spec.md NFR-06, FR-01, FR-02</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="010" status="pending">Persist paraId on ingest — the persisted-id behavior this slice proves.</dependency>
      <dependency task="011" status="pending">Offset-addressing table — the offset→run round-trip this slice proves.</dependency>
      <dependency task="012" status="pending">Opaque atoms — the byte-preserved-atom behavior this slice proves.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec / NFR-06 / ADR-038">The proof MUST be a through-the-wire `WebApplicationFactory` seam slice under `tests/integration/seam/**`. Scope: real endpoint → real DI-wired services → real bytes; unit-green ≠ done.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038 §7">NO `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, NO DI-registration tests, NO ctor-null tests. Scope: this is the vertical-slice-seam KEEP category, not a unit harness — the slice exercises the actual pipeline.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec / FR-01,FR-02">The slice proves all three Phase-1 behaviors: persisted paraIds (load→save→reload), deterministic offset→run round-trip, byte-preserved opaque atoms. Scope: across ≥2 corpus docs.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013 / NFR-05">The slice runs against the real `Services/Compose/` with no AI internals introduced; Tier-1 NetArchTest stays green. Scope: test wiring adds no AI-internal dependency.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / §10 Placement Justification + hygiene">Tests live in `tests/integration/seam/Compose/`. Report BFF publish size absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline, ≤60 MB (test project does not ship, but confirm no BFF-runtime change); verify no new HIGH CVE. Run `/conflict-check` before the BFF PR.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>WebApplicationFactory through-the-wire seam slices; ADR-038 vertical-slice-seam KEEP category; banned mock/DI/ctor tests; Compose ingest/projection endpoints; corpus fixtures</topic>
    <files>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/TEST-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-013-ai-architecture.md</file>
