      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="WebApplicationFactory seam slice" location="tests/integration/seam/">
        Mirror an existing `tests/integration/seam/**` slice: boot the real host, call the real endpoint over the wire, assert on real response/bytes — no `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI-registration assertions.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Corpus-fixture round-trip" location="projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/sample-docs/">
        Drive the slice with real corpus docs (fields/SDT exemplar + a paragraph/offset-rich doc) so the three ingest behaviors and the negative malformed-doc case are exercised on realistic bytes.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Output the FULL rigor-level declaration (note the TEST-MODIFYING override forces FULL gates unconditionally). Load ADR-038 + TEST-ARCHITECTURE + `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`. Confirm tasks 010/011/012 are merged. Run `/conflict-check`.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Create the seam directory + mirror an existing slice">Create `tests/integration/seam/Compose/`. Read an existing `tests/integration/seam/**` slice and mirror its `WebApplicationFactory` bootstrap (real host, real endpoint call, no mocks).</step>
    <step order="2" name="Prove persisted paraIds">Add a slice that loads a corpus doc through the ingest endpoint, saves, reloads, and asserts the same durable `w14:paraId`s are present in the retained bytes (task 010).</step>
    <step order="3" name="Prove offset→run round-trip">Assert the projection's intra-paragraph offset-addressing table maps sample editor-offsets to deterministic `(runIndex, run-local-offset)` run splits (task 011).</step>
    <step order="4" name="Prove opaque-atom byte-preservation">On the fields/SDT exemplar (`01 - Test Matter Create Fields Only.docx`), assert it loads without error and the SDT/field/object subtrees are byte-identical after a no-op save (task 012).</step>
    <step order="5" name="Negative case">Add a malformed / absent-paragraph doc case: assert it still ingests with a minted id and does NOT crash (no unhandled exception; a ProblemDetails or successful minted-id ingest, per the ingest contract).</step>
    <step order="6" name="Run + build + size/CVE">Run the seam slice (green across ≥2 corpus docs + the negative case). Build BFF; confirm no BFF-runtime change; report publish size delta vs ~49.63 MB; `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`.</step>
    <step order="7" name="Close out">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set this task's status to ✅. Document any deviation in `projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a Phase-1 behavior cannot be proven through the wire without reaching for a banned test shape (e.g. the only way to observe the offset table is to mock an internal collaborator), STOP: that signals a seam/observability gap in 010/011/012, not a licence to add a `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;` / DI-registration test. Surface the gap (feed it back to the relevant ingest task) rather than violating ADR-038. Escalate per root §6.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>No through-the-wire seam coverage exists for the new ingest behaviors (paraId persistence, addressing table, opaque atoms).</existing>
    <extension>No — a unit test can't prove the through-the-wire projection contract; ADR-038 seam DoD requires a vertical slice.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>NFR-06 (seam DoD for every load change) has no verifier and ingest regressions ship silently.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <outputs>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/seam/Compose/ — new `WebApplicationFactory` seam slice(s) proving persisted paraIds, offset→run round-trip, and byte-preserved opaque atoms across ≥2 corpus docs + the negative case</output>
    <output type="report">Seam-slice run result; publish-size delta vs ~49.63 MB; CVE scan; confirmation of no banned test shapes</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">A `WebApplicationFactory` seam slice under `tests/integration/seam/Compose/` is green for all three Phase-1 ingest behaviors — persisted paraIds (load→save→reload), deterministic offset→run round-trip, byte-preserved opaque atoms — across ≥2 corpus docs.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a doc with a malformed / absent paragraph still ingests with a minted id and does not crash (no unhandled exception).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The slice uses NO `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, NO DI-registration tests, and NO ctor-null tests (ADR-038 §7 compliant vertical-slice-seam).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The slice runs against the real DI-wired `Services/Compose/` pipeline through the real Compose endpoint (through-the-wire, not unit-mocked).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF builds green; no BFF-runtime change (test project only); publish-size delta reported vs ~49.63 MB baseline; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    No `&lt;justification&gt;` block — this is test coverage for the Phase-1 ingest surface (category =
